},"mime":"application/pdf"}]},"146151697":{"pageid":146151697,"ns":6,"title":"File:Flower Piece - Josina Margareta Weenix - 216 1970.jpg","index":6,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":5822746,"width":2064,"height":2480,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Flower_Piece_-_Josina_Margareta_Weenix_-_216_1970.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":2400,"thumbheight":2884,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Flower_Piece_-_Josina_Margareta_Weenix_-_216_1970.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":2400,"height":2884},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Flower_Piece_-_Josina_Margareta_Weenix_-_216_1970.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flower_Piece_-_Josina_Margareta_Weenix_-_216_1970.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=146151697","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2024-03-07 14:00:09","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"<div class=\"fn\">\nFlower Piece</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"CC-Zero|Author died more than 70 years ago public domain images|Uploaded with pattypan|Artworks without Wikidata item|Images from Royal Albert Memorial Museum and Art Gallery|Artworks with known accession number|CC-PD-Mark|Uploaded by GLAM-E Lab|Paintings in the Royal Albert Memorial Museum|Women Artists (Images from Royal Albert Memorial Museum and Art Gallery)|Josina Margareta Weenix","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nJosina Margareta Weenix</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<p>Dutch artists of the 17th Century became fascinated by the natural world, light effects and perspective. Still-life painting was one aspect of that spirit of enquiry. The main centres for flower painting were Middelburg, Utrecht and Amsterdam and this tradition continued into the 18th century.\n</p>\nApart from famous masters such as Pieter Claesz and Ambrosius Bosschaert, there were numerous painters of still-life whose names are now lost. Real flowers were portrayed with great accuracy but sometimes in impossible arrangements with blooms from all four seasons of the year. Inventive combinations of creatures were often included and here a butterfly, lizard and snail compete for our attention.</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1713<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1713-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"Royal Albert Memorial Museum &amp; Art Gallery","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<table class=\"licensetpl\" style=\"display:none\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span class=\"licensetpl_short\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_long\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_link_req\">false</span><span class=\"licensetpl_attr_req\">false</span>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table style=\"width: 100%; clear: both; margin: 0.5em auto; background-color: var(--background-color-progressive-subtle, #f7f8ff); color: var(--color-base, #202122); border: var(--border-subtle, 2px solid #8888aa); border-spacing: 8px; padding: 0px;\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"layouttemplate\" lang=\"en\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span title=\"Public domain\"><img alt=\"Public domain\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/PD-icon.svg/120px-PD-icon.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" deco